==========================================
  Stateful Ralph Loop - Iteration 1
==========================================

Minor 3 complete. Two targeted improvements to the SDF border shader:

1. **AA band clamping for thin borders**: `border_aa = min(crisp_aa, border_width * 0.5)` prevents the smoothstep transition from consuming more than half the border width at high DPI. A 1px CSS border at 1.5x DPI is only 1.5 physical pixels — the old unclamped AA band (`fw * 0.75 ≈ 1.125px`) ate 75% of it, making borders look soft. Now capped at 50%.

2. **Border highlight gated by `lighting_intensity`**: The 3D directional rim lighting (`border_highlight = 0.025 * ...`) was always applied, ignoring the configurable lighting parameter from Minor 2. Now multiplied by `input.lighting_intensity` so flat CSS-like elements get uniform borders.

Build passes, 19/19 tests pass. Next iteration will pick up Minor 4 (box-shadow spread).

